herrington</surname><given-names>R</given-names></name><article-title>A genome-wide scan of 382 affected sibling-pairs with schizophrenia suggests linkage to chromosomes 2cen and 10p.</article-title><source>Am J Psychiatry</source><year>2002</year><volume>159</volume><fpage>803</fpage><lpage>812</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="doi">10.1176/appi.ajp.159.5.803</pub-id><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">11986135</pub-id></mixed-citation></ref><ref id="B6"><mixed-citation publication-type="journal"><name><surname>DeLisi</surname><given-names>LE</given-names></name><article-title>Critical overview of current approaches to genetic mechanisms in schizophrenia research. Nobel Symposium 111 on Schizophrenia: pathophysiological mechanisms.</article-title><source>Brain Res Brain Res Rev</source><year>2000</year><volume>31</volume><fpage>187</fpage><lpage>192</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="doi">10.1016/S0165-0173(99)00036-3</pub-id><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">10719147</pub-id></mixed-citation></ref><ref id="B7"><mixed-citation publication-type="journal"><name><surname>Malaspina</surname><given-names>D</given-names></name><article-title>Paternal factors and schizophrenia risk: <italic>de novo </italic>mutations and imprinting.</article-title><source>Schizophr Bull</source><year>2001</year><volume>27</volume><fpage>379</fpage><lpage>393</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">11596842</pub-id></mixed-citation></ref><ref id="B8"><mixed-citation publication-type="journal"><name><surname>Ohara</surname><given-names>K</given-names></name><article-title>Anticipation, imprinting, trinucleotide repeat expansions and psychoses.</article-title><source>Prog Neuropsychopharmacol Biol Psychiatry</source><year>2001</year><volume>25</volume><fpage>167</fpage><lpage>192</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="doi">10.1016/S0278-5846(00)00152-4</pub-id><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">11263751</pub-id></mixed-citation></ref><ref id="B9"><mixed-citation publication-type="journal"><name><surname>DeLisi</surname><given-names>LE</given-na